{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV7paletteACvpZ","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"palette","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV","text":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"palette","roleHeading":"Type Property"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"palette","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV","text":"SymbolRenderingMode","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In this mode OpenSwiftUI maps each successively defined layer in the image","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the next of the primary, secondary, and tertiary variants of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"foreground style. You can specify these styles explicitly using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/foregroundStyle(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/foregroundStyle(_:_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modifiers. If you only specify a primary foreground style, OpenSwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically derives the others from that style. For example, you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"render a filled exclamation mark triangle with yellow as the tint color","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the exclamation mark, and fill the triangle with cyan:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Image(systemName: \"exclamationmark.triangle.fill\")","    .symbolRenderingMode(.palette)","    .foregroundStyle(Color.yellow, Color.cyan)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also omit the symbol rendering mode, as specifying multiple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"foreground styles implies switching to palette rendering mode:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Image(systemName: \"exclamationmark.triangle.fill\")","    .foregroundStyle(Color.yellow, Color.cyan)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/symbolrenderingmode\/palette"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A mode that renders symbols as multiple layers, with different styles"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied to the layers."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode\/palette","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/SymbolRenderingMode":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A symbol rendering mode.","type":"text"}],"title":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/symbolrenderingmode","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/do